Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a robust alternative to mean – the median of all 19 models.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the full pool to see if inverse-error weighting improves over median.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test if the best single model (ONLY_DWT_rf) alone outperforms the median ensemble.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ONLY_DWT_rf"}

Thought: Test a simple mean on the smaller, more stable pool1 to see if reducing model set improves performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on the smaller, more stable pool1 to see if removing extremes improves over mean and best_single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool1","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the stable pool1 with inverse_error weighting to see if it beats the best_single model.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a DBA ensemble on the full pool to see if a more sophisticated optimizer can beat the best single model.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a simple mean on the slightly larger pool2 to see if adding a few more models improves over the best_single baseline.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool2"}

